      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485584642": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position: Freelance Computer Programmer – Code Review & System Optimization\nDepartment: Information Technology\nProject: DT Brain\nEmployment Type: Freelance / Project-Based\nReporting To: Chief Technology Officer (CTO)\nCompany: Dany Tameerat\nJob Overview\nDany Tameerat is seeking a skilled and experienced Freelance Computer Programmer to conduct a comprehensive technical review, optimization, and enhancement of DT Brain, the company's integrated business management system.\nDT Brain supports multiple business functions, including Sales CRM, Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, Project Management, Recruitment, and Executive Reporting.\nThe ideal candidate will possess strong programming expertise, with proven experience in reviewing existing codebases, identifying technical gaps, resolving performance and security issues, and implementing sustainable improvements to enhance overall system efficiency, reliability, and maintainability.\nKey Responsibilities\n1. Code Review & Technical Assessment\nConduct a comprehensive review of the existing application codebase.\nIdentify technical deficiencies, vulnerabilities, inefficiencies, and areas requiring improvement.\nProvide a prioritized assessment of recommended fixes and upgrades.\n2. System Performance & Optimization\nIdentify and resolve performance bottlenecks across application pages, database queries, and background processes.\nOptimize database queries, indexing, and overall application responsiveness.\nImprove system efficiency without disrupting existing business operations.\n3. Application Security & Reliability\nAssess authentication mechanisms, role-based access controls, data handling, and software dependencies.\nIdentify and address potential security vulnerabilities in accordance with established web application security practices.\nStrengthen system stability, reliability, and data protection.\n4. Code Quality & System Enhancement\nRefactor and restructure existing code to improve readability, scalability, and maintainability.\nImplement necessary technical upgrades while preserving existing system functionality.\nRecommend improvements aligned with long-term system requirements.\n5. Testing & Quality Assurance\nReview existing automated test coverage and ensure current test suites remain functional.\nDevelop additional tests where necessary to validate system improvements.\nIdentify and resolve defects introduced or discovered during the optimization process.\n6. Technical Documentation & Handover\nMaintain clear documentation of technical findings, modifications, and implemented improvements.\nSubmit a concise technical assessment and completion report.\nProvide recommendations for future system enhancements and maintenance.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nDemonstrated professional experience in software development, programming, and maintaining web-based applications.\nStrong proficiency in one or more programming languages, with the ability to understand and work with existing application architectures.\nPractical experience with Python, Flask, and Jinja-based applications , or demonstrable ability to work effectively with this technology stack.\nStrong understanding of relational databases, including SQLite or SQL-based systems, query optimization, and indexing.\nWorking knowledge of JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nProven expertise in code auditing, debugging, refactoring, performance optimization, and technical troubleshooting.\nFamiliarity with automated testing frameworks, including pytest or equivalent tools.\nUnderstanding of web application security principles, authentication, authorization, and OWASP Top 10.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, documentation, and communication skills.\nPreferred Qualifications\nPrevious experience working with ERP, CRM, finance, or enterprise business management applications.\nFamiliarity with Windows-based server environments and scheduled background processes.\nKnowledge of Node.js or additional web development technologies.\nExperience independently reviewing and upgrading existing business-critical applications.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485704382": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Dengage is a multinational SaaS company dedicated to delivering innovative solutions that drive digital engagement and enhance customer experiences. Our team is passionate about technology and committed to fostering an environment where talent can thrive and grow.\nWe are looking for a talented and motivated Full Stack Developer to join our engineering team and contribute to the development, enhancement, and maintenance of our SaaS platform.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain scalable web applications using modern frontend and backend technologies.\nDevelop responsive, user-friendly interfaces using JavaScript, TypeScript, Vue.js, React, or similar frameworks.\nBuild and maintain backend applications, services, and RESTful APIs using C#, .NET Core, or similar technologies.\nDesign, develop, and optimize relational databases, including SQL Server or PostgreSQL.\nIntegrate frontend applications with backend services and third-party APIs.\nWrite clean, efficient, reusable, and maintainable code following software development best practices.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve application performance and functionality issues.\nParticipate in code reviews, technical discussions, and system design activities.\nCollaborate with product managers, QA engineers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features.\nImplement appropriate security, authentication, and authorization mechanisms.\nWrite and maintain unit tests and integration tests.\nParticipate in Agile/Scrum development processes and contribute to continuous improvement.\nSupport application deployment, monitoring, and ongoing optimization.\nRequirements\nTechnical Skills\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n3–5 years of professional experience in full stack software development.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP), data structures, and software development principles.\nHands-on experience with C#, ASP.NET Core, .NET Core, or similar backend frameworks.\nStrong proficiency in JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML5, and CSS3.\nPractical experience with Vue.js, React.js, or similar frontend frameworks.\nExperience developing and integrating RESTful APIs.\nGood understanding of relational databases, SQL queries, and database optimization.\nFamiliarity with Entity Framework Core or other ORM frameworks.\nExperience with Git and collaborative development workflows.\nUnderstanding of authentication, authorization, and web application security.\nFamiliarity with Agile software development methodologies.\nStrong debugging, analytical, and problem-solving skills.\nGood communication skills and ability to work effectively within a team.\nPreferred / Nice-to-Have Skills\nPrevious experience developing SaaS products or cloud-based applications.\nExperience with Microsoft Azure, AWS, or other cloud platforms.\nFamiliarity with Docker, containerization, and CI/CD pipelines.\nUnderstanding of microservices architecture and distributed systems.\nExperience with Redis, MongoDB, or other NoSQL databases.\nKnowledge of message queues such as RabbitMQ or Kafka.\nFamiliarity with automated testing frameworks.\nExperience working with high-volume data processing applications.\nExposure to marketing technology (MarTech), customer engagement platforms, or customer data platforms (CDP).\nBasic understanding of application performance monitoring and optimization.\nBenefits\nBenefits\nGrowth Opportunities: Access to professional development and career growth within a rapidly expanding SaaS company.\nCollaborative Culture: Work in a supportive and innovative environment where your contributions are valued.\nCompetitive Benefits: Enjoy a comprehensive benefits package.\nD.engage is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all Team Members.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485876213": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Want to learn more about this role and Jobot? Click our Jobot logo and follow\nour LinkedIn page!\nJob details:\nAI Software Engineer, $100,000 to $130,000 base; potential 10% annual bonus, AI-Assisted and Agentic Coding, Support from Senior Engineers\nThis Jobot Job is hosted by: Alex Dickinson\nAre you a fit? Easy Apply now by clicking the \"Easy Apply\" button\nand sending us your resume.\nSalary: $100,000 - $130,000 per year\nA bit about us:\nWe are a digital media business focused on physicians, working at the point where pharmaceutical brands and healthcare professionals meet. Our work centers on building personalized engagement programs that help pharmaceutical brands connect with doctors and other healthcare professionals. Those programs run across multiple channels, so brands can reach clinicians in the places they already spend their time.\nWhy join us?\nCompetitive compensation: $100,000 to $130,000 base; potential 10% annual bonus\n401(k) plan with company match\nComprehensive benefits, including health, dental, life, accident and disability insurance, plus a prescription plan and flexible spending account\nPaid holidays and vacation, along with sick days and a personal day\nHands-on AI-assisted and agentic coding work, backed by senior engineers\nOwnership scope that grows over time\nInternships and personal projects count toward your experience\nJob Details\nYou'll build product features for a digital platform used by physicians, taking on more independent ownership over time, while also helping shape the repository setup and review practices that make AI-assisted and agentic coding dependable.\nKey Responsibilities:\nDeliver product features for the physician-facing platform, growing into more independent ownership as you go\nHelp design software systems and review code written by other engineers\nWrite maintainable applications backed by automated tests, clean code, peer review and clear documentation\nSupport the platform's performance, security and compliance\nSet up the repository context, conventions, automated tests, quality gates and executable plans that keep agentic coding reliable\nExamine AI-generated plans and code with a critical eye and raise any issues you find\nSpot repetitive or time-consuming engineering tasks that can shift to AI-assisted or automated workflows, keeping human review in place where it safeguards quality and compliance\nTrack down and fix bugs in pre-production and production environments, with help from senior engineers\nPartner with engineering and non-engineering colleagues on team and company goals\nTake part in company-wide projects alongside other business units\nNeeded:\nAssociate or bachelor's degree in computer science or a related field, or equivalent software engineering experience\nMinimum 1 year of software development experience (internships, co-ops, academic, open-source or substantial personal projects all count)\nHands-on experience with AI coding assistants, including reviewing and correcting what they produce\nTypeScript\nReact\nPython\nSQL and relational databases\nGit version control\nExperience with at least one major cloud platform (AWS, GCP or Vercel)\nA GitHub profile or portfolio that shows hands-on development work\nAuthorization to work in the US without visa sponsorship\nInterested in hearing more? Easy Apply now by clicking the \"Easy Apply\" button.\nJobot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide an inclusive work environment that celebrates diversity and all qualified candidates receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, national origin, age (40 and over), disability, military status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. Jobot also prohibits harassment of applicants or employees based on any of these protected categories. It is Jobot’s policy to comply with all applicable federal, state and local laws respecting consideration of unemployment status in making hiring decisions.\nSometimes Jobot is required to perform background checks with your authorization. Jobot will consider qualified candidates with criminal histories in a manner consistent with any applicable federal, state, or local law regarding criminal backgrounds, including but not limited to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring and the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.\nInformation collected and processed as part of your Jobot candidate profile, and any job applications, resumes, or other information you choose to submit is subject to Jobot's Privacy Policy, as well as the Jobot California Worker Privacy Notice and Jobot Notice Regarding Automated Employment Decision Tools which are available at jobot.com/legal.\nBy applying for this job, you agree to receive calls, AI-generated calls, text messages, or emails from Jobot, and/or its agents and contracted partners. Frequency varies for text messages. Message and data rates may apply. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. You can reply STOP to cancel and HELP for help. You can access our privacy policy here: jobot.com/privacy-policy\nWant to learn more about this role\nand Jobot?\nClick our Jobot logo and follow our LinkedIn page!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487759912": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Role\nStartupSphere is seeking a Node.js Developer to design, build, and deliver software serving millions of users every day. Based in Anchorage, Alaska, the company is moving toward a remote-native working environment focused on ownership, collaboration, and professional growth.\nThis role offers the opportunity to take ownership of projects, contribute to technology initiatives, and work with a supportive team. The ideal candidate has at least one year of relevant experience, understands technology best practices, and is comfortable taking initiative to identify problems and develop effective solutions.\nKey Responsibilities\nCollaborate with QA teams to define test coverage and identify regressions early.\nMaintain code quality through automated linting, testing, and static analysis.\nIdentify data-driven Interpersonal Skills regressions in staging before they affect Anchorage customers.\nEvaluate existing values-led Interpersonal Skills patterns and recommend cleaner alternatives.\nCoordinate releases with stakeholders across Anchorage, Alaska, and remote teams.\nDevelop Terraform integration tests to identify regressions before releases in Anchorage, Alaska.\nSupport the migration of StartupSphere's Laravel stack out of the Alaska region before the migration deadline.\nRequired Qualifications\n1+ years of relevant experience in technology-related roles.\nStrong attention to detail and the ability to distinguish completed work from work that still needs improvement.\nPattern recognition skills developed through multiple technology engagements.\nAbility to communicate data-driven insights and translate them into actionable decisions.\nAt least one year of experience navigating the challenges and stakeholder dynamics associated with technology projects.\nStrong sense of ownership and accountability for project outcomes.\nSolid understanding of technology best practices and industry standards.\nAbility to take initiative and resolve problems independently.\nCompensation & Benefits\nSalary: $76,000–$109,000.\nGenerous benefits package.\nOpportunities to lead projects and develop professional skills.\nWork Arrangement & Location\nCompany Location: Anchorage, Alaska.\nWork Arrangement: Remote-native working environment.\nLocation Coordination: Collaboration with stakeholders across Anchorage, Alaska, and remote teams.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00"
  },
